WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.434
-Welcome, everybody.
Welcome, welcome.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:04.968
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."
You are here.

00:00:04.968 --> 00:00:06.133
You made it.

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:09.267
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:12.467
This is exciting.
Today is World Teachers Day.

00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:14.667
So thank you to all
the teachers out there.

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:16.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.501 --> 00:00:19.033
Actually, I like World
Substitute Teachers Day

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:21.434
because you just sit in a room
and watch a movie all day.

00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:23.000
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.300
Yep. Every student who gave
their teacher an apple today

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.501
got a B-plus
while everyone who gave them

00:00:27.501 --> 00:00:29.968
an Apple iPhone 15 got an A.
So just saying.

00:00:29.968 --> 00:00:31.200
Just think about it.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:32.534
Guys, listen to this.

00:00:32.534 --> 00:00:35.667
Taylor Swift's Eras Tour movie
comes out next week

00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:38.567
and it's already broken
presale records.

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:39.901
Yeah. That's good.

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:42.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:44.601
So next week,
if you walk past the theater,

00:00:44.601 --> 00:00:46.367
you won't know if the screams
are coming from "Saw,"

00:00:46.367 --> 00:00:47.834
"Exorcist," or Taylor Swift.

00:00:47.834 --> 00:00:49.367
[ Screaming ]

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:51.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.901 --> 00:00:54.300
Of course people are going to
dress up and sing along.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.400
So I guess it's fun
when Swifties do it,

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.300
but when I do it,
I'm "ruining 'Oppenheimer.'"

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:03.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.801 --> 00:01:05.501
Some TV news --
earlier tonight,

00:01:05.501 --> 00:01:09.000
there was a new episode
of "The Golden Bachelor."

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.834
Yeah. All those senior
citizens in one house.

00:01:11.834 --> 00:01:14.300
The medicine cabinet is
the size of a walk-in closet.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:19.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.367 --> 00:01:21.133
Tonight's episode
was kind of slow.

00:01:21.133 --> 00:01:23.133
It was just a full hour
of reminding the Bachelor

00:01:23.133 --> 00:01:24.234
of what happened last week.

00:01:24.234 --> 00:01:26.133
They're like,
"Then you talked to..."

00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:29.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.267 --> 00:01:33.434
Switching -- "I did what?"
"Yeah, you..."

00:01:33.434 --> 00:01:36.033
Switching gears -- some news
from Washington.

00:01:36.033 --> 00:01:39.234
After biting multiple staffers
and Secret Service agents,

00:01:39.234 --> 00:01:41.467
President Biden's dog Commander

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:43.467
has been removed
from the White House.

00:01:43.467 --> 00:01:45.501
[ Audience aws ]

00:01:45.501 --> 00:01:47.834
It's not easy to remove
the White House dog.

00:01:47.834 --> 00:01:49.334
First the House
has to impeach.

00:01:49.334 --> 00:01:53.167
Then the Senate
has to vote to convict.

00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:55.033
On the bright side, Commander
got to split an Uber

00:01:55.033 --> 00:01:56.801
to the airport
with Kevin McCarthy.

00:01:56.801 --> 00:01:58.901
So it's kind of interesting.

00:01:58.901 --> 00:02:00.534
Not bad.

00:02:00.534 --> 00:02:03.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:05.734 --> 00:02:07.601
They actually got Commander
to leave the White House

00:02:07.601 --> 00:02:09.167
the same way they got
Eric Trump to leave.

00:02:09.167 --> 00:02:10.367
They just threw
a tennis ball.

00:02:10.367 --> 00:02:12.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.901 --> 00:02:15.133
[ Barking ]

00:02:15.133 --> 00:02:17.400
[ as Trump ] I remember when
Eric barked for the first time.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:20.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.868 --> 00:02:22.501
[ Normal voice ] Some more news
from the White House.

00:02:22.501 --> 00:02:24.968
The Biden administration
just announced plans to add

00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:27.801
to Trump's border wall in Texas.

00:02:27.801 --> 00:02:28.968
And just to mess with Trump,

00:02:28.968 --> 00:02:30.501
Mexico is like,
"We'll pay for it."

00:02:30.501 --> 00:02:38.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.767 --> 00:02:41.734
"Why not?"
-"Here you go."

00:02:41.734 --> 00:02:43.133
-"We got this one."

00:02:43.133 --> 00:02:45.133
[ Applause ]

00:02:45.133 --> 00:02:47.033
They should.
Well, guys, the number-one movie

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.601
in the country right now
is "Paw Patrol."

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.634
Have you guys seen this?
-Whoo!

00:02:50.634 --> 00:02:52.801
-I haven't seen it yet,
but it looks pretty good to me.

00:02:52.801 --> 00:02:55.334
If you want a quick refresher,
here's the trailer right here.

00:02:55.334 --> 00:02:57.067
-The Paw Patrol is back,

00:02:57.067 --> 00:03:02.267
and this time they're taking
on their scariest villain yet.

00:03:02.267 --> 00:03:05.601
-President Biden's dog
has bitten somebody else.

00:03:05.601 --> 00:03:08.501
It's the Paw Patrol versus
Commander Biden,

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:10.033
now in theaters.

00:03:10.033 --> 00:03:11.167
-What's the dog's name?

00:03:11.167 --> 00:03:13.000
-Commander.
We just said that.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.033
-Yeah, it is.

00:03:14.033 --> 00:03:16.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:16.601 --> 00:03:18.701
Looks good. Looks good.

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:25.367
Hey, get this, guys, I read
that Prada is helping design

00:03:25.367 --> 00:03:29.868
the spacesuits for NASA's
upcoming mission to the moon.

00:03:29.868 --> 00:03:31.634
Can we see the suit?

00:03:31.634 --> 00:03:34.400
Wow, looks pretty cool.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:38.033
-Wow.
Going with the body on top.

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:39.734
-It looks good.

00:03:39.734 --> 00:03:42.667
I think it looks pretty good,
man.

00:03:42.667 --> 00:03:44.501
You guys see this?

00:03:44.501 --> 00:03:49.100
Manhattan's first public beach
just opened downtown. Yeah.

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:51.934
Nothing says beach season like
downtown Manhattan in October.

00:03:51.934 --> 00:03:53.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.901 --> 00:03:55.300
Today, someone built
a sandcastle

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:57.067
and then rented it out
for 5,000 a month.

00:03:57.067 --> 00:03:59.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.968 --> 00:04:02.834
Well, I saw that for Halloween.
Dunkin Donuts has unveiled

00:04:02.834 --> 00:04:05.667
a six-foot-tall inflatable
doughnut decoration.

00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:06.801
Take a look at this thing.

00:04:08.601 --> 00:04:09.734
-Oh!
-Here's something

00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:11.400
I learned today.
Once someone tells you

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:12.734
it looks like
Trump's colonoscopy,

00:04:12.734 --> 00:04:14.934
you can't unsee it.
Don't show it again.

00:04:14.934 --> 00:04:17.801
-Don't look at it.
-You can't unsee it.

00:04:17.801 --> 00:04:19.133
[ Applause ]

00:04:19.133 --> 00:04:21.400
I don't want to look at it.
You'll have to rewind.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:22.467
I'm not --

00:04:24.634 --> 00:04:27.133
And finally, according
to the latest polls...

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:31.133
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:33.434
You can't unsee it.
-Can't unsee it.

00:04:33.434 --> 00:04:35.501
-I didn't do it.
I'm not going to do it.

00:04:35.501 --> 00:04:36.834
According to the latest polls,

00:04:36.834 --> 00:04:38.701
Higgins,
you'll find this interesting.

00:04:38.701 --> 00:04:40.834
-Oh, good.
-Former president Trump still

00:04:40.834 --> 00:04:44.334
leading the Republican primary
with 55% of the vote,

00:04:44.334 --> 00:04:47.801
followed by Ron DeSantis with 13
and Nikki Haley with 8.

00:04:47.801 --> 00:04:49.868
But there's actually a lot
of interesting new data

00:04:49.868 --> 00:04:51.100
about the election.
-Really?

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:52.367
-Yeah, check this out.

00:04:52.367 --> 00:04:53.667
First up, when asked...

00:05:03.834 --> 00:05:04.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:04.834 --> 00:05:07.534
That's how they weighed it.

00:05:11.667 --> 00:05:13.133
Here's another one they asked.
They said...

00:05:21.567 --> 00:05:25.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:25.501 --> 00:05:27.934
I'll try it.

00:05:27.934 --> 00:05:29.033
Up next, when asked...

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:40.434
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.434 --> 00:05:42.033
-Gah.
-Looks like he's getting felt up

00:05:42.033 --> 00:05:44.000
by the TSA or something.
He's like...

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:46.801
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.801 --> 00:05:48.868
Looks like he's waiting
for a ski lift.

00:05:51.067 --> 00:05:52.501
Next up, when asked...

00:06:00.934 --> 00:06:09.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:09.767 --> 00:06:11.133
Here's another one.
When asked...

00:06:17.067 --> 00:06:20.167
[ Laughter ]

00:06:20.167 --> 00:06:23.133
I see it now.

00:06:23.133 --> 00:06:25.033
-You can't unsee it.

00:06:25.033 --> 00:06:27.634
-I'm hearing Yanni.
I don't know.

00:06:27.634 --> 00:06:30.734
When asked...

00:06:38.133 --> 00:06:43.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:43.467 --> 00:06:45.033
Check this one out.
Up next, when asked...

00:06:52.033 --> 00:06:57.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:57.868 --> 00:06:58.901
-Oh.

00:06:58.901 --> 00:06:59.934
-Also when asked...

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:11.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:16.033 --> 00:07:17.200
And finally, when asked...

00:07:22.901 --> 00:07:24.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:24.267 --> 00:07:25.467
We have a great show tonight!

